{"1-2":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":1}],"words":[{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":643},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1079},{"base":"H5068","lemma":"נָדַב","tr":"na·dav","gloss":"be willing","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H5892","lemma":"עִיר","tr":"ir","gloss":"excitement","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1090},{"base":"H7605","lemma":"שְׁאָר","tr":"she·ar","gloss":"remnant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":26},{"base":"H8672","lemma":"תֵּ֫שַׁע","tr":"te·sah","gloss":"nine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":58},{"base":"H1486","lemma":"גּוֹרָל","tr":"go·ral","gloss":"allotted","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":77},{"base":"H6235","lemma":"עֶשֶׂר","tr":"e·ser","gloss":"ten","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":176},{"base":"H1288","lemma":"בָּרַךְ","tr":"ba·rakh","gloss":"to bless","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":330},{"base":"H8269","lemma":"שַׂר","tr":"sar","gloss":"ruler","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":421}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JDG","chapter":5,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"My heart is with the princes of Israel, with the volunteers among the people. Bless the LORD!","from":2},{"book":"ISA","chapter":48,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"who indeed call yourselves after the holy city and lean on the God of Israel; the LORD of Hosts is His name.","from":1},{"book":"ISA","chapter":52,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Awake, awake, clothe yourself with strength, O Zion! Put on your garments of splendor, O Jerusalem, holy city! For the uncircumcised and unclean will no longer enter you.","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":17,"verse":8,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"If a case is too difficult for you to judge, whether the controversy within your gates is regarding bloodshed, lawsuits, or assaults, you must go up to the place the LORD your God will choose. You are to go to the Levitical priests and to the judge who presides at that time. Inquire of them, and they will give you a verdict in the case.","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":24,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"be sure to return it to him by sunset, so that he may sleep in his own cloak and bless you, and this will be credited to you as righteousness before the LORD your God.","from":2},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Joshua cast lots for them in the presence of the LORD at Shiloh, where he distributed the land to the Israelites according to their divisions.","from":1},{"book":"JDG","chapter":20,"verse":9,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now this is what we will do to Gibeah: We will go against it as the lot dictates. We will take ten men out of every hundred from all the tribes of Israel, and a hundred out of every thousand, and a thousand out of every ten thousand, to supply provisions for the army when they go to Gibeah in Benjamin to punish them for the atrocity they have committed in Israel.”","from":1},{"book":"1CH","chapter":26,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They cast lots for each gate, according to their families, young and old alike.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"3-9":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":4},{