ssage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H2705","lemma":"חֲצַר שׁוּעָל","tr":"cha·tsar shu·al","gloss":"Hazar-shual","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H2691","lemma":"חָצֵר","tr":"cha·tser","gloss":"court","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":191},{"base":"H7153","lemma":"קִרְיַת אַרְבַּע","tr":"qir·yat ar·ba","gloss":"Kiriath-arba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H1516","lemma":"גַּיְא","tr":"gay","gloss":"Valley","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":60},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":142},{"base":"H1144","lemma":"בִּנְיָמִין","tr":"bin·ya·min","gloss":"Benjamin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":166}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"(Hebron used to be called Kiriath-arba, after Arba, the greatest man among the Anakim.) Then the land had rest from war.","from":25},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From there Abram moved on to the hill country east of Bethel and pitched his tent, with Bethel to the west and Ai to the east. There he built an altar to the Lord, and he called on the name of the Lord.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So that place was called Beersheba, because it was there that the two of them swore an oath.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":26,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So he called it Shibah, and to this day the name of the city is Beersheba.","from":27},{"book":"GEN","chapter":28,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he called that place Bethel, though previously the city had been named Luz.","from":31},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Cursed be their anger, for it is strong, and their wrath, for it is cruel! I will disperse them in Jacob and scatter them in Israel.","from":36},{"book":"JOS","chapter":8,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Joshua sent them out, and they went to the place of ambush and lay in wait between Bethel and Ai, to the west of Ai. But Joshua spent that night among the people.","from":31},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Therefore Adoni-zedek king of Jerusalem sent word to Hoham king of Hebron, Piram king of Jarmuth, Japhia king of Lachish, and Debir king of Eglon, saying,","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]}}